## 1. Topology
   concept: the partitions of 10 (here two instead of four) each become their own server (a shard); each shard has one primary and N read replicas
   shard 0: primary shard0-primary, replicas shard0-replica-1, shard0-replica-2
   shard 1: primary shard1-primary, replicas shard1-replica-1, shard1-replica-2

## 2. Writes go to the shard's primary
   concept: the router (not Postgres) hashes customer_id to pick the shard; only its primary accepts the write
   alice keyboard -> shard0-primary (id 1)
   alice mouse    -> shard0-primary (id 2)
   bob   screen   -> shard0-primary (id 3)
   carol desk     -> shard0-primary (id 4)
   dave  chair    -> shard1-primary (id 1)
   erin  lamp     -> shard1-primary (id 2)
   check ok: every write went to the primary of the customer's shard, and both shards got writes

## 3. Replicas refuse writes
   concept: a replica replays the primary's WAL and is read-only; there is exactly one writer per shard
   shard0-replica-1 rejected: cannot execute INSERT in a read-only transaction
   check ok: a replica refuses writes

## 4. Reads spread over the replicas
   concept: the router round-robins reads across the shard's replicas; the primary serves no reads
   read alice -> shard0-replica-1: 2 orders
   read alice -> shard0-replica-2: 2 orders
   read alice -> shard0-replica-1: 2 orders
   read alice -> shard0-replica-2: 2 orders
   check ok: reads alternate over the shard's replicas, never the primary

## 5. Replicas are eventually consistent (AP)
   concept: replay paused on shard0-replica-1 to simulate lag: it keeps answering, with old data
   write alice cable -> shard0-primary (committed)
   shard0-primary     3 orders (source of truth)
   shard0-replica-1   2 orders
   shard0-replica-2   3 orders
   check ok: the paused replica still answers, with old data (2 orders); the others have all 3
   shard0-replica-1: WAL received up to 0/5029BD8, replayed up to 0/5029B18 (paused)
   read alice -> shard0-replica-1: 2 orders
   read alice -> shard0-replica-2: 3 orders

## 6. Lag heals
   concept: resume replay: the replica applies the WAL it already holds and converges
   shard0-replica-1   3 orders
   shard0-replica-2   3 orders
   check ok: after resume every replica converges on the primary

